  "description": "Some bikes are designed on a computer. The 8bar DRACHENBERG Ti v1 was developed on real adventures.\n\nWe took the first prototypes of our titanium mountain bike to Nepal, where we tested them on the rugged trails of the Annapurna region. Since then, the DRACHENBERG has carried riders and their gear on demanding bikepacking expeditions and to podium finishes in ultra-distance races.\n\nWe used feedback from those rides and races to refine the bike. Now, after all those miles of testing and development, the DRACHENBERG Ti v1 is finally available to order.\n\nFast on smooth gravel, steady on technical descents and efficient on long climbs, the DRACHENBERG is built for rides that take you across all three. Pack for days in the mountains or line up for your next ultra. Either way, you’ll want to see what’s over the next pass.\n\nFORK VERSATILITY\n\nDesigned around a rigid carbon fork or a 120 mm suspension fork, letting you choose between maximum efficiency or extra confidence on rough terrain.\n\nTITANIUM PERFORMANCE\n\nHandcrafted titanium frame combining low weight, durability, and all-day ride comfort.\n\nSRAM UDH READY\n\nCompatible with the Universal Derailleur Hanger for maximum drivetrain compatibility and future-proof performance.\n\nADVENTURE READY\n\nRack mounts let you carry everything from daily essentials to full bikepacking gear.\n\nCLEAN INTERGATION\n\nFully internal cable routing supports both mechanical and electronic drivetrains for a sleek look and reliable performance.\n\nFIVE MOUNTING POINTS\n\nFive bottle and accessory mounts provide the flexibility needed for long-distance adventures.\n\nFRAME BAG READY\n\nDedicated internal mounts allow a custom frame bag to bolt directly to the frame—no straps required.\n\nT47 BB\n\nModern T47 threaded bottom bracket combines exceptional stiffness with easy maintenance and long-term reliability.\n\n4-PISTON BRAKE COMPATIBLE\n\nDesigned to accommodate powerful 4-piston brake calipers for maximum control on demanding terrain.",
